WEBVTT

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:06.230
These are tsetse flies, 
which transmit sleeping sickness.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.230
<b>Tsetse Fly</b>

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.520
I thought it wouldn't work 
on those mystery animals,

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.240
<b>They fell asleep</b>

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.230
but they fell asleep quite easily.

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:13.740
Oh, that's because I cursed them.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.130
C-Cursed? Are angels allowed to do that?

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.990
Should I not have?

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.640
Operational message!

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.070
Ueda is going to Hell!

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.500
<b>Expelled</b>

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.380
Wh-Wh-What should we do?!

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.430
It's my fault this happened to Ueda-san!

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:36.750
No, it's my fault.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:40.400
Angels are demoted to Hell 
when they use a curse?!

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.010
It's like the epitome 
of divine punishment.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.020
<b>Department: Heaven's Angel Department</b>

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.020
<b>Name                 Ueda</b>

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.020
<b>You are commanded to go to Hell.</b>

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.020
<b>Expelled</b>

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:57.200
Heaven's Design Team

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:34.720
Ueda-san, should we submit our invoice
 for last week's request now?

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:39.670
Do you think Ueda-san really got demoted?

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:43.860
The pandas were our fault, not Ueda-san's.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:45.640
I'll reach out to upper management.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:49.170
We relied on Ueda-san much 
more than we realized, huh?

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.640
It's like that tingling sensation is absent.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.630
Something's missing for sure.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:00.150
O-Oh, we're not saying any 
of this to put you down!

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.650
I know, I really do!

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:05.900
Here you go. I made some cream puffs.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:07.940
I'll go make some tea to go with them!

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.410
What should I do?

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:16.910
Ueda-san's angel communicator 
says she doesn't have a signal.

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:20.560
If Ueda-san doesn't come back...

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.640
No, even by myself, I need 
to do the best I can!

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:37.110
Are you all right?!

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.760
A skull?! The grim reaper!?

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:45.900
An insect?!

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:48.110
I can't do this after all!

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:50.510
Ueda-san!

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.460
Did you call for me?

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:56.880
Did another prototype escape 
from the insect department?

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:00.570
You're quite a big moth.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:03.010
<b>Prototype</b>

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:03.010
The skull pattern on your back is lovely.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:04.750
Ueda-san?!

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:09.890
That "expulsion" was not a demotion, 
it was a business trip.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.240
God did ask me why I used a curse,

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.890
but when I explained that it was necessary 
to prevent work-related deaths.

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:17.510
He didn't reprimand me.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.900
<b>Hell
Sweet
 Buns</b>

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:19.900
I'm so glad!

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:24.140
I hadn't told you about that yet.
Sorry for making you worry.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:28.340
Who knew that lightning bolt was simply 
a way to move around when time is short?

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:30.650
That was bad for my heart.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:32.670
You know there's that new 
venture called "Hell"

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:35.500
that one of the companies associated 
with Heaven is starting, right?

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.250
The project lead there took 
a liking to the pandas,

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:41.300
and wanted to see some material, 
so I was instantly summoned.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.300
<b>Hell</b>

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:44.220
So you really did go to Hell.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.670
That infinitely-multiplying 
panda was truly marvelous.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:52.180
Oh?

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:55.010
I would like to create a 
creature based on that idea,

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:57.940
something that can move even 
without a brain, the "zombie."

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:03.440
I am sure that it will bring 
calamity and fear to the world!

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:05.870
Um, may I ask who you are?

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:08.940
I am the child of darkness 
born from the soil.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:10.960
Oh, pardon me.

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:14.940
My name is Yokota. I recently 
transferred from Heaven to Hell.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:17.330
I used to work for Ueda-san.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:21.330
I am currently working on a 
"theme park of darkness and flame."

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:23.700
This is what it will look like.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.350
It's the exact opposite of Heaven.

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:29.270
It'll be a fun place where you can 
have a taste of anguish and rage,

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:32.210
agony and sloth, thrills and adventure!

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:34.090
I-I see.

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:38.220
<i>He has a scary appearance, 
but he seems dedicated to his work.</i>

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:40.810
So those flames are always 
burning underground?

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.700
Won't they run out of oxygen?

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:46.740
If there's no sunlight, plants can't grow,
so there'll be no food, either.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:51.230
What do these happy gorilla-like
 beings eat? Each other?

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:55.360
As expected, you professionals 
ask the tough questions!

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:00.380
Ventilation

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:00.380
Mountain
(Cross-Section View)

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:00.380
Ventilation

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:57.860
But it won't be underground.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:06:00.380
Main Office

00:05:55.750 --> 00:06:00.380
<b>Theme
\h\h\h\h\hPark
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hInterior</b>

00:05:55.750 --> 00:06:00.380
Entrance

00:05:55.750 --> 00:06:00.380
m 91 254 l 90 291 127 327 168 328 190 297 196 254

00:05:55.750 --> 00:06:00.380
Fully-Equipped
 Employee
 Cantina

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:00.360
Since this is what it'll 
look like, we're fine.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.160
Since we can grow foodstuffs on the outside,

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.380
we will have enough food for our cast.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:09.140
It looks like it's different than 
the Earth we do our work for.

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:13.020
The reason I came by today was 
not just because I wanted to

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:17.420
buy the zombie idea off of you, 
but because I have another request.

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:21.890
I would like you to design a mascot for 
the entrance of our company's theme park.

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:24.890
This is a drawing of what I had in mind!

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.140
A new request?

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:27.910
Yes.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:31.100
Something so flashy that the screams 
of the souls just gush forth,

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:34.420
and so big that it could 
devour us all in one bite!

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:39.410
If it's that big, the design 
will be limited by gravity.

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:45.420
No, please feel free to let your desires 
run free, and prioritize form over function.

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:49.100
In Hell, we can freely adjust 
gravity and oxygen levels,

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.380
so we'll adjust those to the animal.

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.780
But this is...

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:58.940
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:02.750
I shouldn't have dared show my 
drawing to professional designers!

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:04.620
That's not it.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:07.050
The appearance...

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:08.070
The purpose...

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:09.390
The size...

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:11.250
To have so much actual data...

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:13.070
...in a request is so nice!

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:15.070
Let's give it our best shot!

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:16.150
Yeah!

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:19.330
Huh? Yes! Thank you so much!

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:25.090
Then please observe the internal competition 
between the very best designers on our team.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:28.290
The request is for "Hell's mascot."

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:32.640
Then we, Team A, will go first.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:36.350
Just to confirm, this is an 
animal with three heads, right?

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:41.860
Yes! If possible, it should be so terrifying 
and awesome that it chills your blood!

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:45.910
We'll use the wolf that Saturn 
came up with before as a base.

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:47.870
Let's send it over to Mars-san right away!

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:50.850
Here, it's done.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:56.740
It's so cool! It's just 
overflowing with dignity!

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:01.950
The falling-over trope again.

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:04.370
It's bad for my heart, no matter 
how many times I see it.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:08.210
Since each head wants to go 
in a different direction,

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:09.880
the legs get mixed up.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:13.880
<b>Brain</b>

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:13.880
<b>Fakes</b>

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:13.890
Then how about moving the brain 
here and making the heads fake?

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:19.430
I can't really recommend removing 
the brain from the head.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:22.390
The optic and vestibulocochlear nerves
would be more likely to get damaged.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:23.820
Excuse me.

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:24.610
Yes?

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:26.770
As the client, I don't like that, either.

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:31.910
I want to jump into a whirlpool of desire,
 and pet each good boy's head.

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:34.080
That won't work if it's actually
 just one good boy.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.650
The dream is to have multiple good boys!

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:39.650
I want to pet each good boy's head in turn,
 each with his own personality!

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:43.960
Then let's prioritize the middle 
good boy's will for movement.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.200
It's fixed!

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.360
They're walking straight now!

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:51.680
So cool.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.680
Let's try feeding them.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:08:59.240
That's a good appetite!

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:07.470
I put enough for one meal in there.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:10.490
They want to eat three meals' worth.

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:15.280
Wolves do not have a good 
sense of fullness,

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:16.880
so they'll keep eating to their limit.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:18.970
The upside is that they 
are very good at fasting.

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:20.990
They'll get fat for sure, though.

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:24.280
They might become round good boys, 
just like the panda.

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:27.890
Th-That would be cute, but still...

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:31.170
Since they're a mascot, 
they don't need to hunt, right?

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.500
Maybe they should have a 
hobby besides eating.

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:34.480
Hobby?

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:38.810
Playing instruments... is out, 
but maybe they could listen to music.

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:39.890
Sounds good!

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:42.890
<b>Hardcore      Slash Metal      Hip Hop</b>

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.880
If we let them listen to a wide selection 
of genres, they might develop a preference.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:50.770
What's happening?

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:56.780
<b>Break Up</b>

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.430
They're breaking up!

00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:55.150
Apparently they're splitting up because 
of their different tastes in music.

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:56.770
Come on, get along!

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:01.210
Looks like you're struggling, Team A.

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:04.970
This is what we came up with!

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:08.660
It's flying!

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:12.050
Awesome! Its appearance is just 
brimming with murderous intent!

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:15.620
If the gravity is low,
 this design allows it it to fly.

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:17.680
We based the head on the crocodile.

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:20.290
The crocodile? Don't they 
cannibalize each other?

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:22.590
Do not underestimate crocodiles!

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:26.660
They are highly social animals that 
can communicate with their growls.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:28.810
They sometimes even hunt 
in groups by setting traps.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:30.350
Wow...

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:34.810
And while that wolf-type there 
could accidentally become cute,

00:10:34.810 --> 00:10:37.860
this crocodile type has 
a perpetually open mouth.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:41.310
The sharp teeth are intimidating, 
emphasizing how scary it is!

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:43.550
Why are the mouths always open?

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:44.600
Because it's hot.

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:48.640
Just like real crocodiles, the open mouth allows
 water to evaporate, which gets rid of heat.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:50.320
I thought it was for intimidation.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:53.030
Additionally, crocodiles are cold-blooded,

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:56.710
<b>Cold-Blooded</b>

00:10:53.030 --> 00:10:56.730
which means that if you cool them down, 
they shut down and sleep without needing food.

00:10:57.110 --> 00:11:00.210
In other words, if the park is closed, 
it's possible to deactivate them!

00:11:00.650 --> 00:11:03.090
The wolf-type over there is warm-blooded,

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.970
<b>Warm-Blooded</b>

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:05.960
so they'll have to keep eating, 
even if the park is closed.

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:08.980
Ours is cool and economical!

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:11.220
This is Team B's proposal!

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:14.730
Our design's heads accepted each 
other and got back together!

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:18.230
This is a battle of unprecedented intensity!

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:20.470
Yokota-san, what do you think?

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:25.150
If Hell is operational year-round, 
I recommend Team A's warm-blooded wolf-type.

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:30.740
If you will be closed frequently, I recommend
 Team B's cold-blooded crocodile-type.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.860
We haven't decided yet if and 
when the park will be closed.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:36.070
This is just like the sun and moon.

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:40.760
It's just as difficult as having to pick 
either roaring flames or eternal ice.

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:42.760
It's so hard to pick.

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:45.770
Both were accepted!

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:47.760
The fee will be doubled!

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:50.520
<b>Cerberus</b>

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:50.520
<b>Three-Headed
Dragon</b>

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.520
<b>Accepted in Hell</b>

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:50.520
<b>Accepted in Hell</b>

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:52.110
Yay!

00:11:52.110 --> 00:11:53.850
That's so nice.

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:55.090
Oh, that reminds me.

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:59.660
Could I also purchase the skull pattern 
that was on the moth Ueda-san caught earlier?

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:02.100
I was looking for a design to put 
on the T-shirts in the gift store.

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:05.300
Would a payment for the illustration 
plus a royalty contract be acceptable?

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:07.410
I'll go talk to the insect 
department right away!

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:10.210
Wh-What a good client!

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:18.570
There will come a time when I shall 
return again from the deepest darkness!

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.040
I look forward to working with you!

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:28.460
I thought of Hell as a really scary place, but it 
seems like a laid-back place to work.

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:30.270
It looks like they can freely 
pick their own work attire.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:32.840
Oh, it's not that free.

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:40.940
New Hell employees have to design an
 "awesome dark side outfit" for their work attire.

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:42.960
However, but due to budget constraints,

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:45.440
even if it feels embarrassing later,
they are never allowed to change it.

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:48.150
That <i>would</i> be Hell.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:53.580
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:53.200
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:56.360
The bigger ones are about six meters.

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:58.190
That's 3.5 of me.

00:12:58.190 --> 00:13:01.880
These jaws are clearly suited to 
the guardian of the underworld.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:04.330
They use that mouth to chomp babies.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:05.850
It ate it?!

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:10.110
No, the mother is just transporting 
the babies in her mouth.

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:12.340
So crocodiles raise their children?

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:14.220
They do so with the utmost care.

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:19.720
The mother crocodile even sleeps with 
one eye open to watch her children.

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:22.530
They're kinder than they look, huh?

00:13:23.140 --> 00:13:24.980
Just like you, Yokota-kun.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.380
Should we have lunch now?

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:37.860
Yes, this is a good time to stop.

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:40.620
I brought a lunch today!

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:41.870
Me, too.

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:42.880
I'll make some tea.

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:45.100
Thank you, Shimoda-kun.

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:48.350
Two?

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:53.670
Your lunch is so fancy, Venus-kun.

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:57.220
Yours is such a classic.

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:58.630
Compared to that...

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:01.640
It's simple, beautiful and efficient.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:03.710
What's your issue?

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:05.650
That's not appetizing.

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:08.030
The same goes for yours.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:11.190
I'm looking forward, so forward, to lunch!

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:12.040
That's huge!

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:15.430
Come on! That huge thing won't fit here.

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:18.030
The table over there is free.

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:25.310
Ta-dah! Today's lunch is plated on this boat!

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:26.910
Lunch?

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:30.340
I packed it with the freshest 
fruits of the sea.

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:32.440
This glorious shrimp is a test piece.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.040
It's all so fancy.

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:37.850
This is just an aspect of our work, right?

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:39.110
Uh, sure.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:42.690
I collaborated with the insect 
department to make the crab before,

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:44.690
and it turned out really tasty.

00:14:44.990 --> 00:14:46.810
The insect department? The crab?

00:14:46.810 --> 00:14:48.690
That was before you came here.

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:51.980
The crab is like a relative of the insects.

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:56.060
I wanted that tastiness not just 
in crabs, but also in shrimp.

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:59.490
The shrimp is like an elongated crab, 
so I guarantee that it's tasty.

00:14:59.490 --> 00:15:01.840
Shrimp and crabs are also related?

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:05.320
Yes, crabs have their abdomen 
on their underside, right?

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:07.190
The one you can easily open up?

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:10.230
That's just a shrimp tail tucked under.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:15.850
<b>Gastric Mills</b>

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:11.400
Oh, wow.

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:14.910
Shrimp have teeth in their stomach, 
so they chew inside their tummies!

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:21.890
I didn't really want to know that,
 but God has spoken!

00:15:21.890 --> 00:15:23.910
Accepted!

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:24.730
<b>Accepted</b>

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:24.730
<b>Spiny
Lobster</b>

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:27.860
Yay! A big shrimp is born!

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:30.230
It can speak, too.

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:35.400
Oh, sorry.

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:37.240
Should we have lunch, too?

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:39.750
This one is yours.

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:42.600
Oh, you're eating together?

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:43.620
Isn't it cute?

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:47.010
I got an order for an 
"animal that can't swim well,"

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:49.140
so I'm making a fluffy creature.

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:51.150
Fluffy because it can't swim well?

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:54.600
You know how good swimmers 
are all curvy and slippery?

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:58.380
Oh, you're going in the exact opposite 
direction from the dolphin.

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:04.280
That's right. And animals that 
often go into water usually

00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:07.020
have their nose higher up.

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:10.660
This boy's got a small nose 
in the middle of his face.

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:14.500
I left in a lot of land animal features.

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:16.440
And what does he eat?

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:18.280
For now, he's an omnivore.

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:21.280
Stuff like frogs, bugs and grains.

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:23.670
Like frogs...

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:26.800
Since he can't swim well, 
he can't catch fish.

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:30.240
Want to try an urchin?

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:39.560
You can appreciate the flavor of urchin!
 How about a scallop?

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:42.140
Abalone?

00:16:43.780 --> 00:16:44.380
Squid?

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:47.700
What a good boy!

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:50.030
Hey, stop that, Jupiter-kun!

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:52.520
He's bad at swimming!

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:55.300
Look at his cute little pads!

00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:58.560
Tasty seafood comes from 
the cold ocean, right?

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:00.950
He'll bleed body heat through his pads.

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.200
He'll be chilled to the bone!

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:03.790
So that's why this is your food.

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:08.300
Jeez! What will you do if he 
starts preferring seafood?

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:13.190
<i>I'll pretend I didn't see that.</i>

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:15.290
Do you want some lobster?

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:21.430
S-So cute! He's literally beaming!

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:23.770
Oh, man, what should I do?

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:27.890
He can't swim well, but he's fallen 
in love with expensive seafood.

00:17:27.890 --> 00:17:30.690
If cold is the issue, 
he just needs to eat more.

00:17:30.970 --> 00:17:32.960
A gourmet that's also a glutton?

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:36.190
If he just eats a lot, he'll be fine 
because his body temperature will go up.

00:17:36.190 --> 00:17:39.770
There are no sharks in cold oceans, 
and mussels suck at running away,

00:17:39.770 --> 00:17:41.830
meaning it'll work out even 
if he can't swim well.

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:44.330
The secret to survival is eating!

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:47.870
That's no longer the 
animal I came up with.

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:50.400
It's completely under 
Jupiter-kun's influence.

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:52.350
He looks happy, though.

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:57.120
Oh, fine. Want to try going in the ocean?

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:01.470
This looks more like an 
aquarium than the ocean.

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:03.890
It's a simulation space for testing.

00:18:04.590 --> 00:18:10.330
This water is vewy cold. 
My widdle handsies are vewy cold, so...

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.110
<b>Spread</b>

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:15.770
I-It's so adorable!

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:17.960
It's floating on the water!

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:21.750
What? That's so smart! Cute!

00:18:22.020 --> 00:18:26.430
I see. If he raises them up, he can breathe easily
 and his hands don't get cold.

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:31.250
What if we trap air in his coat to 
make his whole body like a life vest?

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:34.880
See? It floats, and since the cold water 
isn't directly touching him, it's not cold.

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:36.250
That's good!

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:38.640
Handsies cold...

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:41.140
Oh, eyesies warm!

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:44.650
Cute!

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:45.660
Adorable!

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.590
Your face can stay like that!

00:18:49.590 --> 00:18:52.760
I'll put the fanciest fur coat on you!

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:56.520
He wears a fancy fur coat and 
gorges himself on fancy food.

00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:57.920
I like that.

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:00.610
So he does have to eat a lot?

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:03.680
With the amount of subcutaneous fat he has,

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:06.660
he has to eat about 25% of 
his body weight to survive.

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:10.160
For your size, that would be
about 15 kilograms of food per day.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:14.670
<b>Rice</b>

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:14.680
This much food... every day?!

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:18.300
So I think he won't have time 
to get back to land to sleep.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:19.720
The fur coat is good,

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:22.440
but if he sleeps while floating on 
the water, he'll be washed away.

00:19:23.230 --> 00:19:24.920
Neptune-san, look at that!

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:27.940
He wrapped kelp around his body!

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:30.800
Th-That's so smart!

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:33.230
What about in regions where there's no kelp?

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:37.310
You should beef up his claws 
so he can hold on to rocks.

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:40.530
Sorry, what did you say?

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:41.320
I was saying the claws—

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:43.770
Neptune-san!

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:47.090
If there's is no kelp, they hold 
hands while they sleep!

00:19:47.090 --> 00:19:49.320
Get out!

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:52.420
Listen, he can't hold a lot of 
food with those small hands.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:53.620
You should enlarge them.

00:19:53.620 --> 00:19:55.080
It's not cute, so I veto that.

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:59.470
I'll give you a pocket, 
so you can carry a lot with you.

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:02.580
P-Pockets? But we need to
 address other issues, too.

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:04.490
Since he was originally a land animal,

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:07.000
eating too much seafood means 
he's getting way too much sodium.

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:08.840
Isn't that your fault?

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:10.720
I understand.

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:14.100
Let's make your kidneys strong, too.

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:17.860
Then you'll be able to 
handle all that sodium.

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:19.990
This is hopeless.

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:23.730
He's stuffing lots of 
mussels into his pockets.

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:26.210
He's so smart!

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:30.620
<b>A Few Days Later...</b>

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:34.950
Is the "animal that can't swim well"
 in the oceans on Earth now?

00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:37.510
Yes, we're testing it on Galapagos.

00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:38.520
Want to come see?

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:39.820
Of course!

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:41.010
I'll come, too.

00:20:45.080 --> 00:20:47.630
Oh, good. They seem well.

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:51.130
Oh, no, this is bad!

00:20:51.590 --> 00:20:53.660
They all have periodontitis!

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:58.290
Always eating hard things 
took a toll on them.

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:00.760
I knew they needed another set of teeth.

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:05.230
You should add teeth in their 
stomachs like shrimp have—

00:21:05.230 --> 00:21:06.220
No!

00:21:06.710 --> 00:21:11.030
But what should I do? 
If you can't eat, you'll die.

00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:12.700
No...

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:21.330
I see, you're using the rock 
instead of your teeth!

00:21:21.330 --> 00:21:23.160
So smart!

00:21:23.160 --> 00:21:24.970
So cute!

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.450
God has spoken!

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:32.230
Accepted!

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:33.600
<b>Accepted</b>

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:33.600
<b>Sea Otter</b>

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:35.720
I'm so happy!

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:38.090
You're coddling him too much.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:38.720
Isn't this great?

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:43.240
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:42.370
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:46.170
Aren't they so cute?

00:21:46.170 --> 00:21:50.010
They are. What's the significance 
of this movement?

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:52.460
That's how they clean their fur.

00:21:52.460 --> 00:21:54.500
In order to protect themselves 
from the cold sea,

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:57.010
it's important that their fur is fluffy.

00:21:57.010 --> 00:22:01.480
I see. So they're making their 
already-fluffy bodies even more fluffy.

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:04.600
The mothers do that fluffing 
for their babies.

00:22:05.190 --> 00:22:07.590
Shimoda-kun, are you ready?

00:22:07.900 --> 00:22:10.590
Yes. As one now, Neptune-san.

00:22:10.840 --> 00:22:13.870
So cute!

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:46.480
<b>Next on the Agenda</b>
